notes: "Before the last slide, the people and projects this work stands on. Three of them are in the code. OpenSlide is the foundation: the editor, canvas, Inspector, presentation and export come from it. Three equation-conversion modules come from OpenPPTD, and PptxGenJS writes the PowerPoint files. Everything else is a relationship of ideas, not code. I first met the PPTD idea in the Kimi Slides ecosystem, and the community open-kimi-ppt-skill notes helped with the format. PowerPoint, WPS and VS Code shaped the workspace: sections, notes, views, tabs and panels. OpenSlides Studio and the OpenPresentation format shaped how objects get stable IDs and how changes are checked against a revision. And I studied PPTist, Slidev, Presenton, PPTAgent and PPT Master as alternatives; each solves part of this problem well, and each taught me something specific. None of them endorses HUANDENG. The full list, with links and what was adopted, is in docs/ACKNOWLEDGMENTS.md in the repository."
